<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
  xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.8.xsd">

  <!--
    DH-011D3 (independent review, §12): the reproducible configuration mechanism for the real
    facility OpenELIS numeric site code. NOT the value itself: that remains NEEDS LIBAN #7,
    never invented anywhere in this repository.

    ${daherOpenelisSiteCode} is populated by LiquibaseConfig.buildChangeLogParameters() from the
    daher.openelis.site.code property (environment-overridable via Spring's standard relaxed
    binding). It is empty in every deployment today, and Java-side validation already rejects a
    non-blank, non-numeric, or still-placeholder value at startup before this changeset ever
    runs; so by the time this file executes, the value is either genuinely empty or genuinely
    a real numeric site code.

    Applies to the SAME row DH-011B originally characterized live: clinlims.site_information,
    name = 'Accession number prefix' (id 106 in the deployment this was authored against),
    domain 'siteIdentity', the same row a human could otherwise set by hand through
    Admin > General Configuration > Site Information. This changeset exists so a fresh
    deployment reaches the same state reproducibly, the same way every other Daher-owned
    Liquibase changeset in this directory replaces a manual admin-UI step with a version-
    controlled one, not because the admin UI path is wrong, but because "someone clicked it
    once" is not a reproducible deployment.

    Fails safely: the precondition below MARKS THIS CHANGESET RAN (not applied, not an error)
    whenever the parameter is empty: the overwhelmingly common case until NEEDS LIBAN #7 is
    answered. No value is invented, and no accession semantics are touched, when the site code
    is still unknown.
  -->
  <changeSet id="daher-011d3-002-site-code-configuration" author="daher-health">
    <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"
        onFailMessage="daher.openelis.site.code not supplied -- leaving the existing accession prefix untouched (NEEDS LIBAN #7)">
      <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">SELECT CASE WHEN '${daherOpenelisSiteCode}' = '' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END</sqlCheck>
    </preConditions>
    <update schemaName="clinlims" tableName="site_information">
      <column name="value" value="${daherOpenelisSiteCode}" />
      <column name="lastupdated" valueComputed="now()" />
      <where>name = 'Accession number prefix'</where>
    </update>
  </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
